# Dev origin — `:3050`, and nothing else

<!--
  Callers: every Cursor/Claude agent session (alwaysApply).
  SoT: AGENTS.md § "Dev origin"; Garisek-OS/scripts/switchboard/server.ts
  User (2026-09-15): "only work from 3050."
-->

**Every request an agent makes to this app goes to `http://localhost:3050`.**
`:3050` is the switchboard: it routes to the pinned lane and stamps
`x-switch-target` / `x-switch-lane` / `x-switch-cookie-scope`. Cookie scoping
(`cf_kiosk` → `cf_kiosk__l7`) happens ONLY through it, so a probe aimed at a
lane port exercises a different cookie namespace than the operator's browser
and can "pass" on state the operator never sees.

## Do

- Curl, Playwright, browser probes, screenshots, smoke tests: `:3050`.
- Lane lifecycle through its unit:
  `systemctl --user {start,restart,status} cycleforge-lane@prod` ·
  `journalctl --user -u cycleforge-lane@prod -f`.
- `:3050` dead or `503` with `x-switch-error`? The LANE is down — start its
  unit. Read switch truth at `GET /__switch/state`.
- Attach, never spawn: `.claude/launch.json` is attach-only by design.

## Refuse

- Probing `:307x`, `:3051`, or any "free port" app server to get around a busy
  `:3050`. `npm run dev` returning `EADDRINUSE` on `:3050` is the switchboard
  working.
- Hand-starting `next dev` on a lane port. That process is unowned, nothing
  restarts it, and it inherits the caller's env — which is how a split-branch
  `DATABASE_URL` once 500'd every DB route.
- Setting `PW_BASE_URL` away from `:3050`, or adding a second dev-server entry
  to `.claude/launch.json`.
- Writing a Neon DSN into a lane env file. DSNs live in the worktree `.env`
  only; the systemd `EnvironmentFile` layer overrides `.env` silently.

## One exception, and it is not an app origin

`request-shape` measures a **production build** on an isolated `NEXT_DIST_DIR`
and a throwaway port, because a dev server reports a different request shape.
Measure there, verify the result at `:3050`, stop it when done, and never build
into the `.next` that `:3050` owns.
